DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260506T163000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260506T171000
SUMMARY:Week 2026-19 - Mobility + Breathing Reset
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: Parasympathetic reset. Correct chest-breathing pattern. Restore hip and thoracic mobility.\n\nHIP FLOW 7 min: 90/90 hip stretch 90 sec each side\, pigeon pose 90 sec each side\, kneeling hip flexor lunge 60 sec each side with posterior pelvic tilt.\n\nT-SPINE FLOW 5 min: Thread the needle 10 slow reps each side\, cat-cow 15 reps full range 3 sec each direction\, thoracic extension over foam roller 60 sec upper back then 60 sec mid back.\n\nANKLE MOBILITY 3 min: Wall ankle stretch 30 sec each side\, banded dorsiflexion 30 sec each side.\n\nTRUNK STABILITY 10 min: Dead bug 3x10 (3-sec lowering\, lower back pinned)\, bird dog 3x10 each side (3-sec hold\, no hip rotation)\, Pallof press 3x12 each side (brace hard before pressing).\n\nDIAPHRAGMATIC BREATHING 8 min: Lie prone (crocodile). Inhale 5 sec nose: belly/lower back expand\, chest still. Hold 2 sec. Exhale 7 sec pursed lips. 4 rounds of 8 breaths\, 30 sec rest between.\n\nKPI: Tension clearly reduced. Breathing feels lower and slower. Evening HRV trend positive.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT90M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Upcoming training session
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rm-2026-19-2@rippedmechanics
DTSTAMP:20260505T123214Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260507T053000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260507T064500
SUMMARY:Week 2026-19 - Swim Technique + Pull Focus
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: Build technique foundation and comfort. No fitness targets — mechanics only.\n\nWARM-UP: 200m easy any stroke\, no effort. Feel neutral buoyancy and water position.\n\nDRILL SET — 6x50m\, 20 sec rest: Rep 1–2 catch-up drill (lead arm fully extended before opposite arm pulls)\, Rep 3–4 fist drill (closed fists to feel forearm\, open fists on 25m swim segment)\, Rep 5–6 bilateral breathing (every 3 strokes\, deliberate).\n\nPULL SET — 8x100m pull buoy\, 15–20 sec rest. HR below 150. Focus: early vertical forearm at entry (fingers point to floor at catch before pulling)\, elbow stays high\, press chest slightly down to float hips up. Count stroke cycles per 25m — target 16–18 (32–36 arm strokes). Above 20 means slipping. Hold or reduce count across the set.\n\nBUILD SET — 4x50m\, 20 sec rest: Rep 1 60% easy\, Rep 2 70% moderate\, Rep 3 80% moderate-hard holding mechanics\, Rep 4 90% hard controlled (note where stroke breaks down).\n\nCOOL-DOWN: 200m easy backstroke or sidestroke.\n\nKPI: Stroke count holds or decreases across pull set. No dropped elbow under fatigue in build set. Breathing bilateral and relaxed.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT90M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Upcoming training session
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rm-2026-19-3@rippedmechanics
DTSTAMP:20260505T123214Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260507T161500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260507T173000
SUMMARY:Week 2026-19 - Run Threshold Intervals
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: Establish threshold HR at true running effort. First structured threshold session.\n\nFUEL: 30–45g carbs 30 min pre-session (e.g. 4 rice cakes + honey).\n\nWARM-UP 15 min: 10 min easy jog building from HR 130 to 150\, A-skip 2x20m\, B-skip 2x20m\, butt kicks 2x20m\, 3 strides building to near-threshold pace (approx 4:45/km on stride 3).\n\nMAIN SET — 4x8 min @ HR 172–178\, 2 min easy jog recovery between reps.\n  Rep 1: Start 4:50/km. Let HR climb naturally by min 2 — do not force it. Target 172–175.\n  Rep 2–3: Adjust pace to hold HR band. Slow 5–10 sec/km if HR > 178. Pick up if HR < 172. Pace is a byproduct\, not the target.\n  Rep 4: Shorten stride slightly\, keep cadence >170 spm. If HR > 180\, immediately slow to 5:20/km until it drops.\n  Recovery: HR must return below 145 within 90 sec. If not\, extend to 3 min and note it.\n\nCOOL-DOWN 10 min: Easy jog fading to walk\, standing quad stretch 45 sec each\, calf 45 sec each\, kneeling hip flexor 60 sec each.\n\nKPI: All 4 reps within HR band 172–178. Pace SD below 10 sec/km across reps 2–4. Form intact in rep 4. Log avg HR and avg pace per rep.
