SUMMARY:Week 2026-19 - Bike Z2 Aerobic
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: Active recovery ride. Preserve legs after Thursday double. Build aerobic base at low cardiac cost.\n\nSESSION — 60–70 min @ 130–170W\, cadence 88–95 rpm throughout. This is recovery-quality riding — no intensity\, no surges.\n\nCADENCE WORK — 5x1 min at 100–110 rpm spread evenly (approx min 15\, 25\, 35\, 45\, 55). Power stays flat in Z2 during cadence reps. 2 min normal cadence 88–92 rpm between each.\n\nBREATHING RULE: Nasal breathing only the entire session. If you cannot breathe through your nose comfortably\, you are going too hard — back off immediately.\n\nCOOL-DOWN: Final 10 min below 130W\, cadence 85 rpm\, spin legs fully loose.\n\nKPI: Avg HR below 145. No cardiac drift across the ride (HR not rising over equal power blocks). Avg power stays inside Z2 range throughout.
