SUMMARY:Week 2026-19 - Long Bike + Short Brick Run
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: Long aerobic bike base. First brick run of the cycle. Race fueling rehearsal.\n\nBIKE — 2.5 to 3h:\n  0–90 min: Pure Z2\, 130–165W\, cadence 88–95 rpm\, HR cap 148. Most important block. If HR drifts above 148 on flat — ease off.\n  90–150 min: Upper Z2\, 165–185W\, cadence 90–95 rpm. HR allowed to 155.\n  150–180 min: Low tempo\, 185–205W\, cadence 92+ rpm\, HR 155–165. Controlled — not a hard push.\n\nFUELING PROTOCOL: Timer every 20 min. Each alert: drink 150–200ml + gel/chew (20–30g carbs). Target 70–90g carbs/hr\, 600mg sodium/hr. Do not rely on hunger.\n\nBRICK RUN — 20 min immediately off bike.\n  Transition within 60 sec. HR will spike to 160–170 — normal. Do not slow to walk. Let it settle. HR below 160 within 3 min — if not\, slow slightly. Conversational effort. Tall posture\, cadence 170+ spm\, relaxed jaw/shoulders. Neuromuscular training\, not cardiovascular.\n\nKPI: Cardiac drift on bike below 10 bpm over equal power blocks in Z2 segment. Brick run HR settles within 3 min. Fueling alarm executed every 20 min — log each fueling event.
