SUMMARY:Week 2026-19 - Long Run Z2
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: The most important aerobic stimulus of the week. Do not compromise this session.\n\nSESSION — 75–90 min. HR cap 150 strict.\n  0–15 min: Very easy\, HR cap 140. Do not start at pace. Ease in\, breathe\, check posture\, feel the feet.\n  15–70 min: Steady Z2\, HR 140–150. Walk any hill that pushes HR above 150 — this is correct aerobic training\, not weakness. Pace will likely be 5:40–6:30/km depending on terrain and fatigue.\n  Final 10 min: Wind down\, HR below 135\, jog fading to walk. Let HR drop naturally.\n\nFORM CUES — check every 10 min:\n  Posture: tall\, slight forward lean from ankles not waist\n  Cadence: 170+ spm (set metronome to 174 if needed)\n  Jaw: relaxed — if tight\, upper body is tight\n  Shoulders: low\, not hunched\n  Glutes: actively driving each stride\n  Breathing: nasal where possible\, rhythmic always\n\nKPI: No HR drift across the 15–70 min middle block. Final km pace within 15 sec of median. Perceived effort conversational throughout. Log avg HR\, avg pace\, and total time in Z2 band.
