SUMMARY:Week 2026-19 - Swim Technique + CSS Prep
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: Reinforce technique from Thursday. Introduce more aerobic load.\n\nWARM-UP: 300m easy mixed strokes. No effort. Focus on water feel and relaxed neck position.\n\nDRILL SET — 8x50m (25m drill + 25m swim)\, 20 sec rest. Cycle through: Rep 1–2 catch-up drill (lead arm fully extended before opposite arm pulls)\, Rep 3–4 fingertip drag (drag fingertips along surface on recovery to enforce high elbow)\, Rep 5–6 6-kick switch (6 flutter kicks between each stroke cycle)\, Rep 7–8 weakest drill.\n\nAEROBIC SET — 6x100m\, 20 sec rest. HR below 145. Target 16–18 stroke cycles per 25m (32–36 arm strokes). 2-beat kick — balance only. Exhale fully underwater before rotating. Head rotation minimal — one goggle in\, one out.\n\nPULL SET — 200m pull buoy easy. Press chest slightly down\, high elbow catch\, feel forearm pressing back through water.\n\nKPI: Breathing every 3 strokes throughout aerobic set. Relaxed neck and shoulders. Hips not sinking. Stroke count stable or decreasing.
